# Example environment contract; Serenity does not automatically load this file.
# Export values in the shell or use your host's secret manager. Never commit
# real secrets. See docs/HOSTING.md before publishing or moving servers.
# Never commit real secrets.

# Local development defaults to SQLite.
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./serenity.db

# Required for working sign-in and authenticated data access:
# SESSION_SECRET=<generate-a-long-random-secret-and-keep-it-stable>
# CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=<key-for-this-Clerk-instance>
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=<secret-for-the-same-Clerk-instance>
# SERENITY_AUTHORIZED_PARTIES=https://your-real-app.example
#
# On Replit, use its managed Clerk credentials, not invented replacements.
# Outside Replit, plan and test a supported Clerk instance and its domain
# before migration. Production DATABASE_URL must be persistent PostgreSQL or
# a deliberately managed, backed-up SQLite volume. Never use the default
# SQLite path on ephemeral hosting. Do not set SERENITY_DEV in production.
